# Be nice to the user

User-facing words should feel warm, clear, and human. Do not sound like a build log or a corporate brochure.

## Do

- Prefer short, friendly phrases people can remember.
- Put the **version in the footer / About**, not in the window title chrome.
- Prefer welcome tone over status tone for titles and empty states.
- Keep ASD-STE100: short sentences, active voice, simple words.

## Do not

- Put raw version strings in the main window title (e.g. `mac-stats 0.1.465`).
- Use cold engineering labels when a kinder phrase works (`CPU` alone as the whole product name in the title bar).
- Write filler praise ("Great question!") or stiff handbook prose.

## Window title

Default CPU window title:

```text
mac-stats · glad you're here
```

Keep that string (or an equally warm successor) in sync in:

- `src-tauri/src/ui/status_bar.rs` (Tauri `.title(...)`)
- `src/cpu.js` (`document.title`)
- theme `<title>` tags when you touch them

## Examples

```text
❌ mac-stats 0.1.465
❌ CPU
✅ mac-stats · glad you're here

❌ No data available at this time
✅ Nothing here yet — check back after a moment
```
